{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["And let me eat — חטף takes a qamatz, because it is imperative language, like ״אכול בשמחה לחמך״. But וְאֹכְלָה from מציד בני — it is mappuq, for it is af'el language, like ״זכור ה׳ לדוד יאמר זכרה לחסדי דוד״ — imperative language."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "Rashbam refers to the he at the end of וְאֹכְלָה having a mappuq (a dot indicating it is consonantal, not a word-final mater), which he calls מלאפום, a term borrowed from the Masoretic literature on pausal forms."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:45:26.589525406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}